1
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,360
<i>You came back</i>
<i>because of that kid last night, right?</i>

2
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,200
I saw him fight just like Arm.

3
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,720
I don't think we can trust him.

4
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:35,840
-I need your help.
-With what?

5
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,400
Look into someone's background for me.

6
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,760
Whose background?

7
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,480
That's Dom.

8
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,600
Who's he meeting?

9
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,280
Fon?

10
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:46,680
Oab?

11
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,440
Do you know him?

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,160
Oab, I just came here to eat.

13
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,440
I ran into a friend.

14
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:55,840
Fon is your ex, right?

15
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,720
No. I never broke up with her.

16
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,040
You know you're acting suspicious, right?

17
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,360
I just want you to know
I haven't done anything wrong.

18
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,840
Everything I'm doing
is because I love you.

19
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,360
The officers said
they're taking everything.

20
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,560
POLICE REPORT

21
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,000
Thirty days? Seriously?

22
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,280
I want you all
to go to bars in other areas.

23
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,920
I want new liquor suppliers.

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,200
Teach them a lesson.

25
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:17,280
No matter where they go,
it has to be my people.

26
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:21,400
You've been away for several days.
Is everything taken care of?

27
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,320
Yes, Sir.

28
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,080
Have you met Fon yet?

29
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:27,040
Not yet.
I came straight here to report in.

30
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,320
Please look after her.

31
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,600
She's new here,
so she probably doesn't know anyone yet.

32
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:33,800
Yes, Sir.

33
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,640
Hey, newbie.

34
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:47,120
I'm Champ. I'll be your partner.

35
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,040
I'm Fon.

36
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,080
Alright.

37
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,720
Right now?

38
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,400
Let's go.

39
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,320
PLAN

40
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,760
We can meet the contract deadlines, right?

41
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,680
Yes.

42
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:12,440
Should I start on the electrical system?

43
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,720
If the structure is finished,
go ahead with the electrical work.

44
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,440
-Bring Chor Thawi Company in as well.
-Yes, Sir.

45
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,560
What are you thinking about?

46
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:45,320
We can't just leave it to Dum
to find suppliers anymore.

47
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:49,880
Thirty days, man.
We'll lose a lot of money.

48
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:53,720
If we don't do something,
we'll be shut down for good.

49
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,960
There are so many drug addicts.

50
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:07,880
Cases where people on drugs
take hostages happen all the time.

51
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:12,640
Hey, Fon. I heard another unit
asked you to help them the other day.

52
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,000
Fon?

53
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:20,760
Yes?

54
00:04:20,839 --> 00:04:22,920
Another unit asked for your help, right?

55
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:28,560
Yes. The Central Investigation Bureau
asked me to help arrest some drug dealers.

56
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:34,840
Are you okay?

57
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,520
You can tell me.

58
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:41,040
We're partners, like family.
We look out for each other.

59
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,720
My boyfriend came to Bangkok.

60
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,640
Isn't that a good thing?

61
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:53,880
Why would it be?
He didn't even tell me he was coming.

62
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,000
I just found out and went to see him.

63
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,280
What did he say?

64
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,640
We just went out for dinner.

65
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,760
Something's bothering me.

66
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:09,280
What is it?

67
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:14,040
He introduced me to the owner of the bar
where he works as just a friend.

68
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,800
Oh, really?

69
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,880
Do you think that's strange?

70
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:24,120
He won't tell me where he lives,
and we can't move in together.

71
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:33,320
He works at a bar. Maybe the owner
doesn't want employees dating?

72
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,840
You're right.

73
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:41,720
But at least I know the bar owner.

74
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,840
You know the bar owner?

75
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:49,280
Yes. Oab was my senior in high school
when I studied in Khon Kaen.

76
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,720
Are you close?

77
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:54,200
Well…

78
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,280
A little.

79
00:05:57,120 --> 00:06:01,040
But last night I forgot to get his number
and ask where the bar was.

80
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,240
How well do they know each other?
Did Fon tell you?

81
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,920
He was her senior from school.

82
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,680
I see.

83
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,200
Could this affect the investigation?

84
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,320
Let's wait and see.

85
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:40,280
<i>It'd be easier to find his bar</i>
<i>if I ask Oab directly.</i>

86
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,280
Excuse me.

87
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,880
Do you have a sanitary pad?

88
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:50,960
It's just that… It started.

89
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:51,880
Oh.

90
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:54,680
-I do. Hold on a second.
-Okay.

91
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,520
Thank you.

92
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:04,240
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I had to get it from my desk.

93
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,520
No worries. Thank you.

94
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,880
What's your name?
I don't think I've seen you before.

95
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,440
I'm Fon. I just started here.

96
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:25,120
I'm Kwang. I work in documents.

97
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,120
You work in documents?

98
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,720
Oh, but you really saved me just now.

99
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,600
If you need anything, just let me know.
I'll help you out.

100
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:41,760
Then are you free tonight?

101
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:44,480
Whoa! What can I do for my savior?

102
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,920
Savior? That's a bit much.

103
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,680
No, seriously.

104
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,880
I was going to invite you to dinner.

105
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:54,440
I've been in Bangkok for a month
and still don't have anyone to eat with.

106
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,960
Sure! I could even eat with you every day.

107
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,720
He is pretty great.
Why did he have to give in to them?

108
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:11,520
Yeah, I thought so too. We're about even.
His side has plenty of people too.

109
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,200
Peng has people backing him up.

110
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,480
Doesn't Oab have people
backing him up too?

111
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,600
Ever since he left their network,

112
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,440
they told everyone to cut ties with us.

113
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:25,840
Wait, Oab used to work for Peng?

114
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,360
Yeah.

115
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,480
Why did he leave then?

116
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,600
They forced him to sell drugs.

117
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,640
Really? Then what did he do?

118
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,919
Hey.

119
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,360
Dom, let's go. Here he comes.

120
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,600
Dom, it's your turn.

121
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:41,039
-Come on. Haw, let's go.
-Yes, Bro.

122
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,440
-Excuse me.
-Yeah?

123
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:48,880
We run a bar.
We're looking for a liquor supplier.

124
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,840
Can I get your number?

125
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,280
Sure. Where's your shop?

126
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,520
Phetchaburi Road.

127
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,120
Why not get supplies from your area?

128
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,240
We're just trying a few different places.

129
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,760
You should look somewhere else.
I don't want any trouble.

130
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,920
Come on.

131
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,800
Can't you help us out?

132
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:11,920
Hey!

133
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:18,640
Don't let me find out
you're supplying liquor to Oab.

134
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,760
Yes, I understand.

135
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:25,040
And tell your guys too.
The boss has strictly forbidden it.

136
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:29,000
Damn, I'm exhausted.

137
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:31,840
If it weren't for the problem
with illegal liquor because of Liang,

138
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:34,800
we wouldn't have to struggle like this.

139
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,960
Come on, Dum.
At least we got one supplier.

140
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:40,800
After going to ten places,
we only got one.

141
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,480
Got what? No way.

142
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:45,280
I called them,
and they won't sell to us anymore.

143
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:48,560
Why not?

144
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,680
Why does everyone have to listen to him?

145
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,600
No one dares go against Peng.

146
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:56,680
If he wasn't really powerful,
he wouldn't have lasted this long.

147
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:03,840
But when you think about it,
Oab isn't someone to underestimate either.

148
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,840
Hey, Oab.

149
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,120
Yes, Boss.

150
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,280
I told you to sell the goods at your shop.

151
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,600
We'll split the profits.
You don't want that?

152
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:21,720
I can't do that.

153
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:24,840
It's money, man. Don't you like money?

154
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:27,760
Of course, I like money,
but I don't want to spend it in prison.

155
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:31,040
I'm ordering you!
Everyone under me follows my orders.

156
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,160
If you don't do what I say,

157
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,920
you can't stay with me.

158
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,360
I really can't do it.

159
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:55,520
Everyone on my side will cut you off.

160
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:59,120
If you think you can survive without us,
then go ahead.

161
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:18,440
<i>But we're still standing.</i>
<i>We can still make a living. In the end,</i>

162
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:20,360
<i>Oab opened a boxing camp</i>

163
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,080
<i>and even knocked out</i>
<i>the number one fighter from Peng's camp.</i>

164
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,720
Arm!

165
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:30,400
The day he took down Arm

166
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:34,680
was the same day he knocked out Man Ocean.

167
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:36,640
Wait.

168
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:39,600
Arm King is Oab's younger brother?

169
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:41,760
Yeah.

170
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,760
So our boss must really hate Peng, huh?

171
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,920
Then why doesn't Oab just take Peng out?

172
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,040
He wants to.

173
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,280
But Peng has a lot of people behind him.

174
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:56,080
If he's going after Peng,
he has to think carefully.

175
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,000
He only gets one chance.

176
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:02,080
Otherwise, Peng will come after all of us.

177
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,520
Thank you so much.

178
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:14,240
You and I are like brothers.
If you need anything, just let me know.

179
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Thank you.

180
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:20,400
But reopening before the 30-day ban ends

181
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:23,480
might be tough. I'll try talking to them.

182
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,440
Okay, let's do this.

183
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:29,680
I just don't want
my bar shut down for good.

184
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:33,280
I'll let you know what happens,
and we'll meet again.

185
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,600
Sure. Thank you so much.

186
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,920
-Let's have a drink sometime.
-Drive safely.

187
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,120
It's 80 baht.

188
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:44,760
No, it's okay. I'll pay.

189
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:47,280
-Hey, let's split it.
-It's fine.

190
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:50,400
-Keep the change.
-Okay.

191
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:55,360
So, does this treat come with a favor?

192
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:01,240
I actually need your help with something.

193
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:05,680
I knew it. You wouldn't suddenly
invite me out for a meal without a reason.

194
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,120
OAB SOMPHAKUL

195
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,320
Can you look into this person for me?

196
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,520
Who is it?

197
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:28,120
A friend of mine.
But he moved to Bangkok when he was young.

198
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,640
Since you moved to Bangkok,
you're trying to find him?

199
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,880
Sure. I'll take care of it.

200
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,120
-Thanks.
-Sure.

201
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:54,040
What brings you here so early?

202
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,160
Pom sent this over for you.

203
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,760
Open it. I'm curious too.

204
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,440
-Hey, Dom.
-What?

205
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,560
I'm out of soap.

206
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,480
Yeah.

207
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:19,360
Ow! I got soap in my eye.

208
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,320
Hey.

209
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:24,560
-Alright, thanks, man.
-Yeah.

210
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,000
Ow.

211
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,960
Hey, what are you doing today?

212
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,720
I'm going to find more suppliers today.

213
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:33,360
I'm coming with you!

214
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,280
Hey!

215
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:36,560
Why are you sticking your head in here?

216
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:39,280
Get out! Get out of here!

217
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,560
Ow! My eyes are burning.

218
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:49,200
I think we should split up.
That way we can find more suppliers.

219
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:53,040
No way! Why split up
and let Peng's guys come after me?

220
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:00,880
Hey, go finish your shower.

221
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:03,760
Wait, I'm going with you.

222
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:06,120
Otherwise,
Peng's guys will bury me six feet under.

223
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:09,600
Finish your shower,
or you're guarding the bathroom.

224
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,200
Come on. I'll wait in the room.

225
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,000
Hey, don't leave without me.

226
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:16,440
No wonder. You used up all the damn soap.

227
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,680
Hey, wait for me!

228
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,400
Hey.

229
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,080
Yes?

230
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:29,320
Get dressed,
then come talk to me in my room.

231
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,880
OAB SOMPHAKUL

232
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,840
Fon, where's Champ?

233
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,560
Probably with the chief.

234
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:55,240
Is the name you gave me your friend?

235
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,120
Why?

236
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,520
Well…

237
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:04,080
Let's go outside.

238
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,080
Come on.

239
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,520
Come here.

240
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,720
Oab Somphakul

241
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:17,000
is an influential figure
that the CSD is investigating.

242
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:18,920
Huh?

243
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,080
Don't be surprised. I'm serious.

244
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:27,080
OAB SOMPHAKUL

245
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,640
<i>As soon as I got in this morning,</i>

246
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,760
<i>I requested</i>
<i>his civil registration records.</i>

247
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:34,440
<i>Once I got them,</i>
<i>I checked his criminal record</i>

248
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:37,960
<i>because I remembered</i>
<i>the name seemed familiar.</i>

249
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,760
<i>So I checked</i>
<i>the list of influential figures.</i>

250
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:45,880
Oab, I just came here to eat.
I ran into a friend,

251
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:48,040
so we talked for a bit.

252
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,520
No wonder he said we were just friends.

253
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,920
Thanks.

254
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,400
-Champ.
-Yeah?

255
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,319
You knew about this too, right?

256
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:09,200
About what?

257
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:10,800
About Dom.

258
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:19,319
You knew too?

259
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,280
I think he's the right person for this.

260
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,760
Can we pull Dom out?

261
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:42,800
No.

262
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,720
But Dom's a boxer, not a police informant.

263
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,320
He agreed to do this himself.

264
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,360
No one forced him.

265
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,680
In exchange for what?

266
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,080
For him to risk his life like this,

267
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:58,240
there has to be something
he's getting in return, right?

268
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:06,800
A stable career.

269
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:11,880
A salary, and benefits equal to yours.

270
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:20,240
Dom is already in.

271
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:23,120
If he pulls out now, they'll find out.

272
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,720
And he will still be hunted down.

273
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,520
If he gets exposed and dies,
who will take responsibility?

274
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:34,320
He has to take responsibility for himself.
He has to survive.

275
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:41,920
What about you? How well do you know Oab?

276
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,200
We used to be close.

277
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,800
But that was back in high school.

278
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:57,640
Then let me give you some advice.

279
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,640
Let Dom finish his mission,

280
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,280
and make sure this never gets out.

281
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,080
At least can you give me Dom's address?

282
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,840
I don't think that's a good idea.

283
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,320
You don't trust me to keep this secret?

284
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:35,000
He is my husband.
Do you really think I'd risk his life?

285
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:38,400
What if you make a mistake?

286
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,560
A lot of people
we've sent in before got caught

287
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,200
and never made it back out.

288
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,560
Have a seat.

289
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,880
I had someone look into your background.

290
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,400
Yes.

291
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:27,120
You only moved
to Ban Haet a few years ago.

292
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,080
Yes.

293
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,320
Your wife died?

294
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:37,880
Oh.

295
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,040
Yes, Oab.

296
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,360
Your records say you don't have a wife.

297
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:53,600
Well…

298
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:57,560
We lived together,
but we weren't legally married.

299
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:07,200
So you quit boxing because…

300
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:09,760
your wife died.

301
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:12,400
Yes. I just didn't have the heart
to fight anymore.

302
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:19,560
If I asked you to box seriously again,
would you do it?

303
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:21,760
Yes, Oab!

304
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:30,760
I mean, if you believe I can do it
and you want me to,

305
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,600
I'll come back and fight for you.

306
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:35,840
Good.

307
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,880
-But…
-But what?

308
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:43,800
I'd still like
to keep working at the bar too.

309
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:49,200
I don't have a problem with that.
Just try to manage your time.

310
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:01,760
How's Dom's cover story?

311
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:04,400
I've taken care of it.

312
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:08,920
He only moved to Ban Haet a few years ago.
He's single and has never been married.

313
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:12,440
If they check his background,
there shouldn't be any problems.

314
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:22,960
Dum, this is a big deal, isn't it?

315
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,240
I don't know either.

316
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:29,920
Let's go, Pong.

317
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,680
What happened?

318
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:38,360
What did Oab say?

319
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:40,200
Nothing much.

320
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:41,480
-Hey.
-Hey.

321
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,200
-Dom.
-Dom.

322
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,120
Calm down.

323
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:47,680
What is it?

324
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:48,800
Did he kick you out?

325
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,840
-Who's gonna help me mop the floor?
-Is it serious?

326
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,400
He wants me to…

327
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,720
take boxing seriously.

328
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:04,920
Take boxing seriously?

329
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:09,640
Wow, you really dragged this out.

330
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:13,200
That's good news!
You had me worried for nothing.

331
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,760
-Yeah.
-Geez.

332
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:19,600
Why did he ask you to box
but never asked me?

333
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:24,720
-Ask you to box? Someone like you?
-Yeah.

334
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:25,680
Yeah.

335
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:26,600
Here you go.

336
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:29,080
Go wipe down the sandbags.

337
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:31,680
You can't even run properly,
and you wanna box?

338
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:34,360
Bro, you know boxing is my dream.

339
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,440
A dream?

340
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:38,440
-Whoa, a scrawny guy like you?
-I'm training.

341
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:40,400
Haw, if you're free,

342
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:41,760
-you can train with me.
-I'm in!

343
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:44,960
Wait. Are you sure
he won't just become a burden to you?

344
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:48,240
Having a training partner is still better.
At least I won't be lonely.

345
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:50,040
See? I told you.

346
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:51,840
He picked the right coach.

347
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,640
But you still have to work
at the bar, right?

348
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:01,680
Of course.

349
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:03,800
Hey, we should celebrate!

350
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,640
No more looking for liquor suppliers.

351
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,040
Let's celebrate!

352
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:10,680
-Let's celebrate!
-Let's celebrate!

353
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:12,880
Celebrate?

354
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:15,440
That's all you wanna do. Get to work, Haw.

355
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:17,280
-Go!
-Yes.

356
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:19,000
Let's go. Come on, follow me, Haw.

357
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:20,480
-Yes.
-Go work.

358
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:21,720
Yes.

359
00:24:30,120 --> 00:24:33,480
According to the records Pom found,
Dom is an orphan.

360
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:38,000
But the other day,
I saw him step outside to make a call.

361
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:40,080
He said he was calling his mom.

362
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:44,160
Maybe he just looks up
to someone like a mother figure?

363
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:48,200
I've warned you,
but you're not listening to me at all.

364
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:52,600
I'm listening.
I had Pom investigate Dom's background.

365
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:54,000
But did we find anything?

366
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,880
I'm just afraid
you're trusting the wrong guy.

367
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:16,920
Oab.

368
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,000
Fon.

369
00:25:23,760 --> 00:25:24,880
What are you doing here?

370
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:32,000
I was going to come to this bar,
but I just saw that it was closed.

371
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:33,880
Oh.

372
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:37,480
You own this bar?

373
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:39,320
Yes.

374
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:42,320
Aren't you working today?

375
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:44,520
I'm off today.

376
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,280
Uh, actually…

377
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,120
The bar got shut down for 30 days.

378
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:51,800
But since you're already here,

379
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:53,520
do you want to go for a walk?

380
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:57,720
We haven't seen each other in years.
I have a lot to talk to you about.

381
00:25:58,680 --> 00:25:59,880
Hey.

382
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:02,640
You can head back.

383
00:26:02,720 --> 00:26:04,360
-Oab.
-Just take my car.

384
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:07,040
Let's go.

385
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:20,320
How are your parents doing?

386
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:22,120
They're doing well.

387
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:24,280
Sometimes I think
they're even stronger than me.

388
00:26:27,600 --> 00:26:30,160
What about your mom? How is she?

389
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:34,000
My mom passed away

390
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:36,560
a few years after she went to prison.

391
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:40,400
I'm sorry.

392
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:42,440
What are you sorry for?

393
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:45,080
For asking about your mom.

394
00:26:45,160 --> 00:26:47,720
It's okay. You didn't know.

395
00:26:48,600 --> 00:26:50,600
You never contacted me.

396
00:26:56,280 --> 00:26:59,960
I didn't want you to see me like that.
It was embarrassing.

397
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:02,720
Why would you be embarrassed?

398
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,840
I wanted you to see
that you could rely on me.

399
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:11,160
When I moved into the foundation,

400
00:27:12,560 --> 00:27:13,720
I felt like…

401
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:18,000
I couldn't even take care of myself.

402
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:21,080
How could you rely on me?

403
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:32,280
He never listens.

404
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:35,160
He never cared about anyone.

405
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,400
But after meeting this cop,

406
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:39,600
it's like he's under a spell.

407
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:43,080
SKATE RENTAL

408
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,600
SHOE STORAGE

409
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:57,080
How do I bring it up?

410
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:07,680
Do you know how to skate?

411
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,040
No, I don't.

412
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:16,960
Oab, I'll put them on myself.

413
00:28:17,040 --> 00:28:17,880
It's okay.

414
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:20,520
If you can't skate,
how will you put them on? Let me do it.

415
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:23,720
Come on.

416
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:47,080
I got one point, Oab.

417
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:52,120
Are you okay?

418
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:53,560
It hurts a little.

419
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:54,480
PLAIFON SAISOMBAT

420
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:56,920
But I'm more embarrassed.

421
00:28:58,360 --> 00:28:59,640
Why be embarrassed?

422
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:02,440
Come on. Let's sit down.

423
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:10,480
Oh no, my shoe!

424
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,680
Well? You wanted to win so badly
that your shoe tore.

425
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:21,360
It's ripped like this.
How are you gonna get home?

426
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:23,680
I guess I'll walk home barefoot.

427
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:31,240
Why are you taking off your shoes?

428
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:32,920
Are you going to walk home with me?

429
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:36,920
Hey!

430
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:42,360
You'll walk home barefoot like this?
Your feet will hurt like crazy.

431
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:45,320
What about your feet?

432
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:46,760
I'll be fine.

433
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:50,520
Let's go home.

434
00:29:53,600 --> 00:29:55,000
Are you sure you can walk?

435
00:29:55,080 --> 00:29:56,240
Easy.

436
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:15,720
Come on.

437
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:19,920
-Walk slowly.
-Okay.

438
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:22,760
Just walk for now.

439
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:35,720
Geez.

440
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,560
Guess I don't have to worry
about you getting jumped.

441
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:40,360
I'm more worried
I'll go blind from diabetes.

442
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:42,200
I can't handle this.

443
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,320
You're pretty good.

444
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:55,360
If your bar is closed like this,
Dom must be out of work, right?

445
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:58,520
No. I'm thinking
of having Dom take up boxing.

446
00:30:59,120 --> 00:31:00,160
You have a boxing camp too?

447
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:01,120
Yeah.

448
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:05,080
-What's your camp called?
-King Camp.

449
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:07,560
-Wait, King Camp?
-Yeah.

450
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,640
You know it?

451
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:12,280
I do. Where is it?

452
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:15,360
Want to go? I'll take you there.

453
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:21,680
I mean, if you're free,
you could stop by and see me sometime.

454
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:27,600
Sorry, I mean…

455
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:30,560
Are you free today?

456
00:31:36,360 --> 00:31:37,600
I am.

457
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:41,400
You just moved here,
so no friends yet, right?

458
00:31:49,360 --> 00:31:51,000
-Want to continue?
-Okay.

459
00:31:56,920 --> 00:31:58,240
BUS STOP

460
00:32:37,520 --> 00:32:40,040
You should've stayed out of it.

461
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:55,040
You helped him,
but no one's gonna help you.

462
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:10,960
Why is he taking so long?

463
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:18,000
-Pong!
-What is it?

464
00:33:18,720 --> 00:33:20,120
Boss Kiat got stabbed badly.

465
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:23,600
It must've happened
when he helped Oab with the bar issue.

466
00:33:24,280 --> 00:33:27,880
It was Peng.
He must've known Boss Kiat helped Oab.

467
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:30,480
What should we do, Bro?

468
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:34,080
Damn it.

469
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:38,520
I heard Liang is waiting at the bar
to take us on.

470
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:42,880
You get the sales,

471
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,680
and I get liquor to sell.
Good deal, right?

472
00:33:45,280 --> 00:33:48,560
I heard Boss Peng ordered everyone
not to supply your boss's bar.

473
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:50,080
If I do it, won't I be in trouble?

474
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:52,280
Hey, you won't get in trouble.

475
00:33:52,360 --> 00:33:53,320
Hey!

476
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:55,640
What are you doing with my supplier?

477
00:33:56,800 --> 00:33:59,600
Nothing. We're just talking.

478
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,280
Nothing, my ass.

479
00:34:02,440 --> 00:34:04,160
You guys are trying to steal my supplier.

480
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:07,840
The boss said to deal with you

481
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:10,480
if we see you.

482
00:34:24,639 --> 00:34:25,679
Hey, where are you going?

483
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:27,440
-Something happened to Dum!
-What?

484
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:28,960
Something happened to Dum!

485
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:32,440
Pong, what happened?

486
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:33,880
Dum and Dom got jumped.

487
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:36,080
I'm coming with you.

488
00:34:36,159 --> 00:34:37,560
-Fon, wait here.
-I'm coming too.

489
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:39,120
Fon, stay here.

490
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:40,840
Got the weapons yet?

491
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,920
Haw!

492
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,000
-Haw!
-Come on!

493
00:37:24,080 --> 00:37:25,440
Come at me!

494
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:34,520
Dom, get Haw to the hospital.

495
00:37:35,040 --> 00:37:36,720
-Come on. Haw, get up!
-Yeah.

496
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:50,800
-Ouch.
-Come here!

497
00:37:56,560 --> 00:37:57,680
Pong!

498
00:38:08,640 --> 00:38:09,800
Watch out, Bro!

499
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,080
Get in the car.

500
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:54,320
Hey, Haw! Stay with me!

501
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:56,440
Hurry up! My friends got shot.

502
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:01,200
Hang in there.

503
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:08,560
-Agh!
-Come on.

504
00:39:22,880 --> 00:39:25,120
EMERGENCY

505
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:55,120
Today was really…

506
00:40:07,480 --> 00:40:08,360
Hey.

507
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:11,320
I haven't told you about Boss Kiat yet.

508
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:13,160
Why? What happened to him?

509
00:40:16,320 --> 00:40:17,240
Peng's guys got him

510
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:20,920
when he went to help us with the bar.

511
00:40:22,880 --> 00:40:25,800
They're backing us into a corner,
forcing us to sell their drugs.

512
00:40:28,240 --> 00:40:29,240
Damn it.

513
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:34,760
Give me the money!

514
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,800
No, this is our kid's tuition money!

515
00:40:36,880 --> 00:40:38,840
Then don't pay the damn tuition!

516
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:41,720
No, we can't.
This is our kid's tuition money!

517
00:40:42,320 --> 00:40:43,640
-Give it back!
-Give it to me!

518
00:40:47,920 --> 00:40:49,360
You think you can stand up to me?

519
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:53,200
No, Dad!

520
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:55,760
-Don't.
-What the hell?

521
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:57,000
Dad, stop!

522
00:41:11,920 --> 00:41:14,040
Oab!

523
00:41:15,680 --> 00:41:16,880
Oab, my dear.

524
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:19,840
Mom…

525
00:41:31,120 --> 00:41:33,440
-Oab, my dear.
-Mom.

526
00:41:34,120 --> 00:41:35,720
-Mom.
-I'm the one who did this.

527
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,840
It's alright, dear.

528
00:41:54,120 --> 00:41:55,680
No matter what, I'm not selling.

529
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:59,400
Even if it kills me, I won't sell.

530
00:42:59,240 --> 00:43:01,160
Why are you guys hurt this badly?

531
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:04,960
Peng's guys attacked us.

532
00:43:12,880 --> 00:43:14,600
Did everyone make it back?

533
00:43:14,680 --> 00:43:15,920
Uh…

534
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:19,280
Some of them got shot,
so they had to go to the hospital.

535
00:43:24,600 --> 00:43:26,880
-But no one died, right?
-No one died.

536
00:43:30,840 --> 00:43:31,680
Then…

537
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:34,560
you guys could go to a hospital?

538
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:41,720
I've been donating to that hospital
through the foundation.

539
00:43:41,800 --> 00:43:45,040
So they take care of my people in return.

540
00:43:47,160 --> 00:43:48,640
What hospital is that?

541
00:43:48,720 --> 00:43:50,200
Thiennapa.

542
00:43:52,200 --> 00:43:54,200
Then I'll get going.

543
00:43:54,800 --> 00:43:55,640
I'll take you.

544
00:44:10,120 --> 00:44:12,040
Oab, you can drop me off here.

545
00:44:14,320 --> 00:44:15,280
Uh…

546
00:44:17,320 --> 00:44:18,800
Can I have your number?

547
00:44:54,320 --> 00:44:57,200
This is my number.
Call me if you need anything.

548
00:44:58,800 --> 00:45:01,000
You're alone here.
You should have someone, right?

549
00:45:05,800 --> 00:45:06,640
Are you uncomfortable?

550
00:45:09,360 --> 00:45:12,520
I'm just afraid you'll get annoyed
if I call you too often.

551
00:45:13,840 --> 00:45:15,440
If it's you, I won't get annoyed.

552
00:45:45,560 --> 00:45:47,240
Taxi!

553
00:45:49,200 --> 00:45:51,000
To Thiennapa Hospital, please.

554
00:46:02,400 --> 00:46:04,280
Ow, doctor.

555
00:46:06,520 --> 00:46:07,360
Doctor, wait.

556
00:46:08,280 --> 00:46:09,360
Sorry.

557
00:46:17,440 --> 00:46:18,520
Sorry.

558
00:46:54,840 --> 00:46:55,840
Excuse me!

559
00:46:57,280 --> 00:46:59,080
This person is my relative.

560
00:47:38,960 --> 00:47:39,960
I'm sorry.

561
00:47:46,160 --> 00:47:47,520
Oab's guys came here, right?

562
00:47:53,680 --> 00:47:55,960
I'm asking you. Answer me.

563
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,720
They're here, aren't they?

564
00:47:57,800 --> 00:48:00,520
This is a hospital.
Please don't cause trouble.

565
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,200
Then take me to them.

566
00:48:03,280 --> 00:48:04,320
Stop!

567
00:48:05,640 --> 00:48:07,480
You should listen to the staff.

568
00:48:13,200 --> 00:48:17,120
Those guys in there shot my men.

569
00:48:23,120 --> 00:48:25,360
I assume your side shot them too.

570
00:48:52,080 --> 00:48:54,080
Cops aren't allowed to shoot first, right?

571
00:48:55,000 --> 00:48:58,920
I'll just go to court.
Since you have a gun, I'll be fine.

572
00:49:00,560 --> 00:49:03,440
But I'll definitely shoot you.

573
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:34,240
-Fon.
-Dom!

574
00:49:53,240 --> 00:49:55,120
I couldn't find you in the ER. I thought…

575
00:50:02,040 --> 00:50:03,560
When I got shot,

576
00:50:05,960 --> 00:50:07,600
I was so scared.

577
00:50:11,120 --> 00:50:13,280
I was scared
I'd never see your face again.

578
00:50:28,600 --> 00:50:30,400
It hurt a lot, didn't it?

579
00:50:32,200 --> 00:50:33,640
I'm sorry.

580
00:50:38,280 --> 00:50:41,720
I'm sorry I lied about what I was doing.

581
00:50:41,800 --> 00:50:44,760
Dom, it's okay.

582
00:50:49,240 --> 00:50:50,920
But I can't back out now.

583
00:50:52,360 --> 00:50:53,960
You understand, right?

584
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:02,000
Why did you take this job?

585
00:51:07,200 --> 00:51:09,160
I want to grow old with you.

586
00:51:11,680 --> 00:51:15,160
I want us to take care
of each other until the end.

587
00:51:21,520 --> 00:51:25,480
I know your dad doesn't like me

588
00:51:26,080 --> 00:51:29,360
because he thinks I'm living off you.

589
00:51:31,680 --> 00:51:35,000
When he complains to you,
you have to listen.

590
00:51:35,880 --> 00:51:38,720
You can't do anything,
and you can't tell me.

591
00:51:39,840 --> 00:51:41,400
It's hard being caught between us.

592
00:51:42,520 --> 00:51:43,720
I understand.

593
00:51:47,520 --> 00:51:49,680
That's why I want to finish this job.

594
00:51:50,680 --> 00:51:53,960
If I become a government employee,
I'll have a stable career.

595
00:51:59,240 --> 00:52:01,680
Maybe your dad
will start to feel better about me.

596
00:52:33,480 --> 00:52:34,440
What happened today

597
00:52:36,640 --> 00:52:39,000
should clear your doubts about Dom.

598
00:52:48,920 --> 00:52:50,360
If it wasn't for him,

599
00:52:51,120 --> 00:52:52,240
I wouldn't have made it.

600
00:52:55,120 --> 00:52:56,160
Yeah.

601
00:52:58,720 --> 00:53:00,280
I don't have a problem with him anymore.

602
00:53:13,480 --> 00:53:15,840
What about Peng? What are you gonna do?

603
00:53:23,600 --> 00:53:24,920
I think it's time.

604
00:53:26,600 --> 00:53:28,720
Find a way to bring Liang over to me.

605
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:41,720
POL. MAJ. GEN. SAENCHAI SAENSUWAN

606
00:53:41,800 --> 00:53:43,920
I'd like permission
to help Dom with this mission.

607
00:53:45,640 --> 00:53:46,840
No.

608
00:53:46,920 --> 00:53:50,720
But he was almost killed last night.
If we do nothing, he could die.

609
00:53:52,520 --> 00:53:54,960
He already agreed to take on this mission.

610
00:53:55,040 --> 00:53:57,840
That means he accepted the risks.

611
00:53:59,120 --> 00:54:00,360
But he might not realize

612
00:54:00,440 --> 00:54:03,640
how dangerous it is
to work with powerful people.

613
00:54:12,280 --> 00:54:15,520
Since we can't cancel the mission,
let me go in.

614
00:54:16,040 --> 00:54:18,040
I'll finish it as quickly as possible.

615
00:54:31,520 --> 00:54:33,040
Why did you just get here?

616
00:54:34,080 --> 00:54:37,360
I've been here for a while.
I was just talking to the chief.

617
00:54:44,320 --> 00:54:45,600
About Dom?

618
00:54:48,480 --> 00:54:51,920
From now on,
if you get any updates on this case,

619
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,280
let me know too.

620
00:54:54,840 --> 00:54:56,080
Is the chief okay with that?

621
00:54:57,120 --> 00:54:58,760
I'm joining this case too.

622
00:55:20,240 --> 00:55:21,320
-Fon.
-Huh?

623
00:55:21,840 --> 00:55:23,000
I'm hungry.

624
00:55:26,560 --> 00:55:28,240
You still haven't had breakfast?

625
00:55:31,640 --> 00:55:34,680
Is eating during work hours
really a good idea?

626
00:55:38,120 --> 00:55:40,120
Then let's buy some and eat at our desks.

627
00:55:40,200 --> 00:55:41,120
-Okay.
-Come on.

628
00:55:41,720 --> 00:55:43,480
Can't you go by yourself?

629
00:55:51,720 --> 00:55:54,800
Excuse me, I invited Fon, not you.

630
00:55:54,880 --> 00:55:57,560
Go ahead and work yourself
to death at your desk.

631
00:55:57,640 --> 00:56:02,320
You love your job so much.
Hope you get promoted seven ranks at once.

632
00:56:03,120 --> 00:56:04,360
Let's go.

633
00:56:10,880 --> 00:56:12,680
Seven ranks?

634
00:56:17,240 --> 00:56:18,960
Are you really cursing him to death?

635
00:56:19,040 --> 00:56:20,640
Yeah. He annoys me.

636
00:56:21,280 --> 00:56:23,040
So what is it?

637
00:56:23,640 --> 00:56:24,960
It's urgent.

638
00:56:26,840 --> 00:56:29,760
A police station
called Oab in for questioning.

639
00:56:33,800 --> 00:56:35,920
-You seem different, Bro.
-How so?

640
00:56:36,000 --> 00:56:37,760
You've been smiling more lately.

641
00:56:37,840 --> 00:56:38,880
I'm happy.

642
00:56:40,280 --> 00:56:41,880
You need to get a grip, Oab.

643
00:56:41,960 --> 00:56:44,720
With Dom and the police,
you can't let your guard down like this.

644
00:56:44,800 --> 00:56:46,520
Don't get involved with those two.

645
00:56:46,600 --> 00:56:49,120
I know exactly what I'm doing.

646
00:56:49,200 --> 00:56:50,080
Oab is here.

647
00:56:55,680 --> 00:56:56,920
COME MEET ME

648
00:57:04,840 --> 00:57:07,520
-Who the hell are you?
-What are you doing here?

649
00:57:07,600 --> 00:57:09,040
-Pong!
-What are you doing here?

650
00:57:09,640 --> 00:57:11,640
It's been years
since we last saw each other.

651
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:14,000
Maybe I'm not the person
you used to love anymore.

652
00:57:14,080 --> 00:57:17,200
Whether it was ten years ago,
today, or ten years from now,

653
00:57:17,280 --> 00:57:19,240
I'll always love you the same, Fon.

654
00:57:53,360 --> 00:57:54,200
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
